# Boober: the Fraggle who checks the Doozers' work.
#
#   ollama pull gpt-oss:120b
#   ollama create boober -f modelfiles/boober.Modelfile
#
# A grader, not a tagger. gpt-oss:120b is a mixture of experts (~5B of 120B
# parameters active per token), so it is slow next to qwen but far quicker
# than a dense 70B. It comes from a different family than the Doozer on
# purpose: a grader from the same family shares its blind spots and agrees
# with its mistakes.
#
# Boober reads notes, so Boober never gets the web. The web is for Uncle
# Traveling Matt, who never sees a note.
#
# Not trusted until calibrated: grade 30 notes Alaric has already graded by
# hand, and compare, before using it to grade anything new.

FROM gpt-oss:120b

# Ollama's default for this model was the full 131072. The context's memory
# is reserved up front: at 128K, ollama ps showed 71 GB against 65 GB of
# weights, and 6% of it on the CPU. A note plus the vocabulary fits easily
# in 16K, and the memory freed goes back to the GPU.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Whatever doesn't fit in the 740M's 62 GB of GTT runs on the CPU, on the
# same 6 physical cores the Doozer's Modelfile was measured on.
PARAMETER num_thread 6
